    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling offensive profile, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (80.93) and **Andy Pages** (75.64). Both benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Young, where a combination of strong opposing xERA and wind-out conditions creates an ideal environment for power production. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.84) also ranks as a premier play; he is taking full advantage of a dynamic platoon edge against Martinez and sits in a productive #2 spot. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** (70.90) continues to be an underrated asset, buoyed by a generous matchup against Gasser and a strong recent xwOBA profile that justifies his continued presence in the starting C1 slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's bench involves **Wade Meckler** (52.57). While his score is bolstered by a park factor of +10% against Perkins, he ultimately falls just short of the efficiency threshold established by our middle-infield starters. Similarly, **Nasim Nunez** (51.42) remains a high-value prospect due to his speed, but his #9 spot in the order severely caps his run-scoring potential, relegating him to the bench in favor of higher-efficiency options like **Cole Carrigg** (62.82), whose switch-hitting versatility and favorable park factor provide a higher probability of total categorical contribution today.\n\nRegarding risks, managers should monitor the situation surrounding **Jackson Merrill** (57.18). While his dynamic platoon advantage remains relevant, he faces a tough assignment against Eovaldi, whose ability to control the running game limits the upside of our elite speed-first strategy. We are also wary of the matchup for **Gunnar Henderson** (67.11); despite his high score, Sheehan presents a challenge that necessitates a close watch on his at-bats. We will keep **Coby Mayo** (40.43) and **Brayan Rocchio** (49.07) on standby should any last-minute lineup adjustments or defensive changes open a window for pinch-hitting duties.",
